---
title: Custom audio
description: How Paper Mario DX organizes audio files, how your mod overrides them, and how names in those files become constants in your code.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

You add or replace sound effects, instruments, songs, and ambient sounds by putting files in your mod's `audio` folder. When you build, DX combines your files with the game's audio, and gives each sound, song, and ambient sound a constant, such as `SOUND_SHOP_BELL`, that your code uses to play it.

## What is in the audio folder

The game's own audio is split from your ROM the first time you build, as source files you can read and copy. Your mod uses the same layout.

| Path | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| `audio/sfx/` | The sound effects, a file each, named after their sounds |
| `audio/sfx/envelopes/` | The press envelopes that sequenced sound effects share, a file each |
| `audio/songs/` | The songs, as `.bgm` files that you edit in [Mamar](https://mamar.bates64.com), each named after its song |
| `audio/mseq/` | The ambient sounds, as MSEQ files named after their sounds, and the radio's four stations |
| `audio/bank/NAME/` | A sound bank: a `sound_bank.xml` file and a WAV file for each sample. It's always loaded unless a song or the radio loads it. |
| `audio/presets.xml`, `audio/drums.xml` | Instruments and drums that songs select by ID |

[Star Rod](/papermario-dx/star-rod) has an Audio Booth that previews samples, sound effects, and ambient sequences, including the ones your mod adds.

## How your files override the game's

Audio uses the layers that [Project structure](/papermario-dx/project-structure) describes. A file in your layer replaces the game's file at the same path, and a new file in `audio/sfx/`, `audio/songs/`, or `audio/mseq/` adds a sound, song, or ambient sound. To delete a file, put `delete: true` in `<file>.meta` next to it. To delete a directory, such as a bank, put it in `.meta` inside the directory.

## Names and constants

Sounds, songs, and ambient sounds are named after their files. The build uppercases the file name and adds a prefix:

| Folder | Prefix | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `audio/sfx/` | `SOUND_` | `coin_pickup.xml` becomes `SOUND_COIN_PICKUP` |
| `audio/songs/` | `SONG_` | `toad_town.bgm` becomes `SONG_TOAD_TOWN` |
| `audio/mseq/` | `AMBIENT_` | `lava_1.xml` becomes `AMBIENT_LAVA_1` |

File names must start with a lowercase letter and contain only lowercase letters, digits, and underscores.

